    ///   <para>emmo:EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13 : A world entity is direct causally self-connected if any two parts that make up the whole are direct causally connected to each other. In the EMMO, topological connectivity is based on causality.
    /// All physical objects, i.e. entities whose behaviour is explained by physics laws, are represented only by items. In other words, a physical object part is embedded in a direct causal graph that provides always a path between two of its parts.
    /// Members of a collection lack such direct causality connection, i.e. they do not constitute a physical object.
    /// Following graph theory concepts, the quantums of an item are all connected together within a network of causal relations, forming a connected causal graph. A collection is then a set of disconnected graphs.</para>
    ///   <para>skos:prefLabel : Item</para>
